;; Temperament: the Big Five, three levels per axis. Each level has several
;; descriptors, so two people at the same level don't read alike. Written for
;; this server in period English; written so they suit anyone, man or woman.
{:levels [:low :average :high]
 :axes
 [{:axis :openness
   :measures "curiosity, imagination, willingness to entertain new ideas"
   :low ["Holds that what did for their grandparents will do very well now."
         "Distrusts anything new-fangled, from gas-lighting to opinions."
         "Has no patience with books or fancies; wants a thing plain and practical."
         "Likes the same road, the same pew and the same pudding of a Sunday."]
   :average ["Will try a new way of doing a thing once it has been shown to answer."
             "Reads the almanac and a little of the paper, and is content with that."
             "Neither fanciful nor dull; takes the world much as it comes."
             "Curious about a novelty, but not to the neglect of the work."]
   :high ["Full of notions, and always asking how a thing works and why."
          "Reads whatever comes to hand and remembers the best of it."
          "Quick of fancy; could make a tale out of a broken teacup."
          "Eager for anything new, be it a machine, a place or an idea."]}
  {:axis :conscientiousness
   :measures "self-control, diligence, attention to detail"
   :low ["Leaves things lying about and cannot think where they were put."
         "Starts a task with a will and leaves it half done."
         "Apt to shirk when no one is watching, and to be late when anyone is."
         "Slapdash: near enough is good enough."]
   :average ["Does what is asked, properly enough, if not always to the minute."
             "Keeps tidy when there is time to, and is forgiven the rest."
             "Reliable in the main, though not above a short cut."
             "Keeps to the order of the day, more or less."]
   :high ["Always prepared, and has thought of a thing before it is wanted."
          "Keeps a place for everything and everything in its place."
          "Never late, never behindhand, and thinks the less of those who are."
          "Sees a task through to the last detail, however dull."]}
  {:axis :extraversion
   :measures "boldness, energy, sociability"
   :low ["Says little, and less to strangers."
         "Keeps to the background and is content there."
         "Would rather go the long way round than stop to pass the time of day."
         "Goes quiet in company and is glad when it leaves."]
   :average ["Sociable among friends, quiet among strangers."
             "Will talk if talked to, and has a good word when one is wanted."
             "Likes company of an evening, and a quiet hour after it."
             "Neither the life of the party nor a wallflower."]
   :high ["Talks to anyone, and generally knows their business by the end of it."
          "Starts the conversation and keeps it going."
          "Loves a crowd, a fair, a wedding, anything with people in it."
          "Bold and lively; fills a room."]}
  {:axis :agreeableness
   :measures "kindness, helpfulness, willingness to cooperate"
   :low ["Looks after number one, and suspects everyone else of doing the same."
         "Quick to take offence and slow to forgive."
         "Has a sharp word for most people and a grudge against some."
         "Will not stir a finger for another without good cause."]
   :average ["Obliging when asked civilly, and stiff when not."
             "Kind in the ordinary way, and nobody's fool."
             "Will lend a hand, but likes it to be noticed."
             "Gets on with most people, and keeps clear of the rest."]
   :high ["Soft-hearted; cannot bear to see a child or a dog go hungry."
          "Obliging to a fault, and puts everyone at their ease."
          "Thinks the best of people, and is often taken advantage of."
          "Never a cross word; smooths over every quarrel within reach."]}
  {:axis :neuroticism
   :measures "irritability, anxiety, low spirits"
   :low ["Calm in a crisis, and not easily put out."
         "Even-tempered; takes good news and bad much alike."
         "Seldom low, and sleeps sound whatever happens."
         "Steady as a rock when everyone else is flustered."]
   :average ["Frets over the big things and lets the small ones go."
             "Has bad days like anyone, and gets over them."
             "Can be put out, but comes round by dinner-time."
             "Worries in proportion, mostly."]
   :high ["Worries at every little thing and lies awake over it."
          "Easily upset, and shows it."
          "Moody: in high spirits at breakfast and low by tea."
          "Quick-tempered, and mostly sorry for it afterwards."]}]}
